            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nNo, there is currently no way to set this permanently. The suggested way is to:\n- Use `V` explicitly for Visual mode selection.\n- Force mode in Operator-pending mode. Example with the following setup:\n\n    ```lua\n    local ai = require('mini.ai')\n    ai.setup({\n      custom_textobjects = {\n        F = ai.gen_spec.treesitter({ a = '@function.outer', i = '@function.inner' }),\n      },\n    })\n    ```\n\n    Typing `dVaf` will delete `@function.outer` match linewise instead of charwise (default).\n\nIt is possible to add `opts.vis_mode` to `gen_spec.treesitter()` to pass down to [created regions](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/7bbafa4691147bc8b74a51986b957daca14c1876/doc/mini-ai.txt#L190-L192). One problem here is that this will affect both captures and it will be impossible to force charwise mode (like `dvif` won't work to force charwise mode).\n\nI'll think about this (as adding `opts.vis_mode` is relatively straightforward), but I am currently leaning to suggesting to use explicit mode forcing (as it is more versatile) or going the `Vaf`-`d` route.",
