        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "After thinking about it, I think I am going to close this. The `opts.vis_mode` solution will probably be not enough, because I can see how `a` and `i` textobjects having different values (like linewise `a` but charwise `i`) can be useful. But allowing it to be more granular than for both captures is a bit too much.\n\nInstead I'd keep suggesting approaches from the previous comment (explicit Visual or forced Operator-pending modes). Another approach is to manually create custom textobject with something like this:\n\n```lua\nlocal ai = require('mini.ai')\nlocal ts_linewise = function(captures)\n  local ts_charwise = ai.gen_spec.treesitter(captures)\n  return function(...)\n    local regions = ts_charwise(...)\n    for _, r in ipairs(regions) do\n      -- NOTE: This can also be done more granularly, like only for `a`\n      -- textobject (check first argument of `...`).\n      r.vis_mode = 'V'\n    end\n    return regions\n  end\nend\n\nai.setup({\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    F = ts_linewise({ a = '@function.outer', i = '@function.inner' }),\n  },\n})\n```",
            "created_at": "2025-09-14T11:51:11Z",
